WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.069
And not even the Orthodox Easter

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:03.837
could bring a halt

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:05.138
to the fighting in Ukraine.

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:07.140
On Sunday, Ukrainian forces said

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.074
Russia had unleashed

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:09.809
an almost almost 100

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:11.511
shells of the past 24 hours

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:13.980
around back boats with around 30

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.782
firefights taking place.

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:17.250
Ukrainian and Russian fighters

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.085
are battling street by street

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:19.486
and house

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:20.920
by house for control of

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.156
what's now a pretty decimated city.

00:00:23.323 --> 00:00:24.157
And there was, of course,

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:26.026
little joy on this Easter holiday.

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:28.862
130 Ukrainians are now free

00:00:29.129 --> 00:00:30.697
after a prisoner exchange with Russia.

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:32.799
So that at least is some good news.

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:34.000
But there are many Ukrainians

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.735
who may never come home.

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:36.736
At the start of the war.

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:37.804
They fled

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:39.105
in the only direction that they could

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:40.407
and that was into Russia.

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:41.141
Now they're living

00:00:41.141 --> 00:00:42.642
thousands of miles away

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:44.177
in Russia's Far East.

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:45.045
CNN Scott McLean

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:46.613
established contact with some of them

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:48.114
who describe their lives now

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:50.383
and why Ukrainians may not want them back

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:54.621
in the chaos of battle in

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:55.855
Mariupol, in eastern

00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:56.489
Ukraine,

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:57.557
the civilians caught in

00:00:57.557 --> 00:00:59.626
the crossfire had few good options.

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:01.694
They could either escape to Russia

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:03.129
or take their chances

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:05.098
as the war intensified.

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:06.499
Many of those who fled toward

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:07.700
Russia were encouraged

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.836
to live and work in the Far East.

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:10.737
From Rostov,

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:11.905
a 4000

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:12.939
mile train journey

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:15.175
to the edge of Siberia and a town

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:17.577
just a stone's throw from North Korea.

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:21.081
These are some of the first arrival

00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:22.215
stepping off government

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:24.584
chartered trains a year ago.

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:27.620
Why does Russia want those people there?

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:28.855
That's a great question.

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:31.524
One is a propaganda benefit

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:33.893
Positioning these people as somehow

00:01:34.461 --> 00:01:37.564
willingly seeking citizenship in Russia.

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:40.667
The second benefit is that Russia

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:42.035
simply needs bodies

00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:44.037
in many parts of the country.

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:45.839
They don't have enough citizens

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:47.941
to make those municipalities function.

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:51.244
This hotel in the coastal town of Wrangel

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:52.679
was where new arrivals

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:54.347
will put up at first.

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:55.181
CNN reached

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:57.283
several of them through a telegram group

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:59.519
chat run by local volunteers,

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:01.621
keeping a log of resident requests

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:04.124
from baby food and toys to medicine.

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:07.227
Anyone dissatisfied with their stay

00:02:07.227 --> 00:02:08.795
is told sarcastically

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:11.030
to take their complaints to Moscow.

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:12.432
The Kremlin. Putin.

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:13.967
The Russian

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:14.601
government has

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:15.368
long been eager

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:17.971
to populate its resource rich Far East,

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:19.205
and the state has tried

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:20.306
several experiments

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:21.674
to attract settlers,

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:23.910
including those from ex-Soviet states.

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:26.946
It now promises fleeing Ukrainians cash,

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:29.149
housing assistance, citizenship

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:30.850
and even free land

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.352
Though two people told CNN

00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:33.286
they were struggling

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:34.854
to get the rent reimbursement

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:37.524
they say the government had promised.

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:38.758
Natalia was struggling

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:41.027
to find any housing at all,

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:43.396
hardly enthused by her new reality.

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:45.331
From, you know,

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:47.433
nothing's changed except the place.

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:49.235
But I no longer have a job that I love

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:51.204
in a home that I love more crack

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:52.238
rather than pop.

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:53.072
New arrivals

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:54.407
quickly had their Ukrainian

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:56.409
passports swapped for Russian ones.

00:02:56.743 --> 00:02:59.312
Natalia figures she can't go back

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:00.613
it's almost only

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:02.582
because we are criminals there,

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:04.117
because those who left for Russia

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:04.951
are immediately

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:05.985
considered criminals

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:07.954
by the Ukrainian authorities.

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:09.989
So I'm forbidden to go there

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:11.191
at this point.

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:13.126
The absence of clarity

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:14.694
is the biggest problem

00:03:14.694 --> 00:03:17.730
there is, understandably, within Ukraine,

00:03:18.131 --> 00:03:20.767
a absolute outrage

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:22.535
against those

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:24.571
who are perceived as collaborators.

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:25.972
But the fact of the matter is

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:27.540
that we are dealing here

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.442
with the civilian population

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:34.013
that was seeking refuge in a time of war.

00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:36.916
Under the terms of Russia's

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:38.151
relocation program,

00:03:38.151 --> 00:03:39.886
the Ukrainians are required

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:42.121
to stay for at least three years.

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:44.123
One woman, Marina, told CNN

00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:46.159
that after that, we will see.

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:47.660
It depends on the job

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:49.262
and material well-being.

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:51.631
So far, it's not very easy.

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.633
Another Valeria said plainly

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:55.735
that her family will stay in Russia.

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:57.403
And I don't even want to think

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:59.339
about Ukraine.

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:00.173
In a statement,

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:01.341
the Ukrainian prosecutor

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:02.208
general's office

00:04:02.208 --> 00:04:03.610
told CNN that safety

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:05.044
and security of Ukrainian

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:07.213
citizens is a major priority

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:09.649
and that for many the only safe passage

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:11.050
was through Russia.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:11.618
Of course,

00:04:11.618 --> 00:04:13.720
they are not considered collaborators.

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:14.887
They need to get to a third

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:15.855
country and address

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:17.724
a local Ukrainian consulate.

00:04:17.724 --> 00:04:18.691
It will issue them

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:21.094
Ukrainian documents to return to Ukraine.

00:04:22.462 --> 00:04:24.197
But for those who remain in Russia

00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:26.799
long term, the future is less clear

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:28.268
by Ukrainian law.

00:04:28.268 --> 00:04:30.536
People who publicly deny occupation

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:32.138
or who call for support

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:33.573
for Russian actions

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:35.908
are considered collaborators.

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:37.410
International law prohibits

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:39.379
forcible transfers of people.

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:41.581
Russia says more than 5 million

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:43.283
Ukrainians have arrived in Russia

00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:45.485
since the full scale war began.

00:04:45.485 --> 00:04:46.786
And while Ukraine says

00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:48.921
many were forcibly deported,

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:50.923
some, like Oksana, said they

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:51.758
went willingly

00:04:52.759 --> 00:04:54.260
civil by nature.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:54.560
We were

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.396
saving our own lives,

00:04:56.396 --> 00:04:59.399
though they had few other options.

00:04:59.399 --> 00:05:01.100
And Scott McClain joins us now.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.635
Scott, did any of the individuals

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:04.170
that you and your teams spoke to?

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:04.771
Did they tell you

00:05:04.771 --> 00:05:06.806
that they'd been forcibly deported? Yes.

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:09.275
And no one that we spoke to told us that.

00:05:09.275 --> 00:05:10.343
And they all insisted

00:05:10.343 --> 00:05:11.811
that they had gone by choice.

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:12.545
But also, remember that

00:05:12.545 --> 00:05:13.613
we're talking about a group of people

00:05:13.613 --> 00:05:15.114
that is, by and large, working class.

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:15.782
They speak Russian.

00:05:15.782 --> 00:05:16.749
They have no ties to Europe.

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:17.350
And so

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:18.184
going to Russia

00:05:18.184 --> 00:05:19.285
for most people was simply

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:21.220
the path of least resistance.

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:22.488
It is also very unlikely

00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:23.956
that anyone that we spoke to

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:24.691
will be going back

00:05:24.691 --> 00:05:26.592
to Ukraine any time soon.

00:05:26.592 --> 00:05:28.361
They are allowed to go.

00:05:28.361 --> 00:05:30.129
They're free to leave if they wanted to.

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:31.431
But if they stay for

00:05:31.431 --> 00:05:32.932
less than three years in Russia,

00:05:32.932 --> 00:05:33.800
they'll have to pay back

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:35.268
the state benefits that they've gotten,

00:05:35.268 --> 00:05:37.236
which is out of reach for most people.

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:38.604
So now the big question mark is

00:05:38.604 --> 00:05:40.573
what happens after three years

00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:41.941
and by then will Ukraine

00:05:41.941 --> 00:05:43.443
even want them back?

00:05:43.443 --> 00:05:44.677
It's also impossible to know

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:46.179
just how freely people felt

00:05:46.179 --> 00:05:47.280
that they could speak with us.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:48.448
But you got the impression

00:05:48.448 --> 00:05:49.182
from some of them

00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:51.217
that they were on the side of Russia.

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:54.020
One woman told us that she

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:54.687
you know, as

00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:56.255
the Ukrainians who are responsible for

00:05:56.255 --> 00:05:57.457
what happened in Mariupol,

00:05:57.457 --> 00:05:57.824
in other words,

00:05:57.824 --> 00:05:58.958
said that she wanted to go back,

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:00.727
but only if it was firmly in the hands

00:06:00.727 --> 00:06:01.861
of the Russians.

00:06:01.861 --> 00:06:02.995
By then,

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:04.497
other people had more nuanced views

00:06:04.497 --> 00:06:05.932
or didn't want to talk about the war.

00:06:05.932 --> 00:06:06.899
I should also say quickly

00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:07.934
that we did also reach out

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:08.868
to the Russian Ministry

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:09.736
of Internal Affairs,

00:06:09.736 --> 00:06:11.304
but we didn't get any responses

00:06:11.304 --> 00:06:12.705
to our questions from them.

00:06:12.705 --> 00:06:14.474
Scott, thanks so much for joining us.

00:06:14.474 --> 00:06:16.409
Ben, great to have you with us.

00:06:16.409 --> 00:06:18.511
The city of Mahmoud still,

00:06:19.078 --> 00:06:20.079
I guess, hangs.

00:06:20.079 --> 00:06:21.581
It hangs in the balance

00:06:21.581 --> 00:06:23.449
and fighting is intensifying.

00:06:23.449 --> 00:06:24.417
Could you tell us

00:06:24.417 --> 00:06:25.585
what the latest lines are

00:06:27.987 --> 00:06:28.921
Yeah, I

00:06:28.921 --> 00:06:29.622
learned that

00:06:29.622 --> 00:06:31.758
Mahmoud is just barely hanging

00:06:31.758 --> 00:06:32.959
in the balance at this point.

00:06:32.959 --> 00:06:34.427
But first, let me explain to you

00:06:34.427 --> 00:06:35.194
where I am

00:06:35.194 --> 00:06:37.163
where in Sloviansk in eastern Ukraine,

00:06:37.163 --> 00:06:38.064
not far from

00:06:38.064 --> 00:06:39.932
not in front of that building

00:06:39.932 --> 00:06:43.536
that last Friday was hit by an S-300

00:06:43.536 --> 00:06:46.105
Russian surface to air missile.

00:06:46.639 --> 00:06:48.574
The workers are still clearing away

00:06:48.574 --> 00:06:49.675
the rubble.

00:06:49.675 --> 00:06:50.777
This was the worst

00:06:50.777 --> 00:06:53.079
single strike on Sloviansk

00:06:53.079 --> 00:06:55.248
since the beginning of the full scale

00:06:55.248 --> 00:06:58.684
Russian invasion more than a month ago.

00:06:59.185 --> 00:07:01.487
15 people were killed in that strike

00:07:01.487 --> 00:07:03.122
as far as Mahmoud goes.

00:07:03.122 --> 00:07:04.724
The fighting is intensifying

00:07:04.724 --> 00:07:06.192
the Russian Ministry of Defense

00:07:06.192 --> 00:07:07.126
has put out a statement

00:07:07.126 --> 00:07:07.994
claiming that

00:07:07.994 --> 00:07:09.729
two new districts

00:07:09.729 --> 00:07:11.998
have been taken in back mount.

00:07:12.031 --> 00:07:12.632
And really,

00:07:12.632 --> 00:07:13.266
the fighting

00:07:13.266 --> 00:07:15.168
there is the most intense

00:07:15.168 --> 00:07:17.270
in the entire front.

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:19.071
And what we saw the other day

00:07:19.071 --> 00:07:19.839
is that

00:07:19.839 --> 00:07:20.640
the authorities,

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:23.309
the police are trying desperately

00:07:23.509 --> 00:07:24.811
to convince people

00:07:24.811 --> 00:07:26.879
who are living in those areas

00:07:26.879 --> 00:07:28.948
to move away from the fighting

00:07:29.148 --> 00:07:31.017
as quickly as possible.

00:07:33.186 --> 00:07:35.221
Another family is moving out,

00:07:35.822 --> 00:07:36.856
leaving the frontline

00:07:36.856 --> 00:07:38.424
town of Krasnodar, Rivka,

00:07:38.424 --> 00:07:41.360
with the help of the police,

00:07:41.527 --> 00:07:42.962
perhaps to lessen the blow

00:07:42.962 --> 00:07:44.063
to his children.

00:07:44.063 --> 00:07:46.032
Yevgeny quips, We'll be back.

00:07:46.032 --> 00:07:48.334
It's just a vacation.

00:07:48.334 --> 00:07:50.303
84 year old Raya doesn't

00:07:50.303 --> 00:07:51.971
sugarcoat it.

00:07:53.739 --> 00:07:55.741
It's like torture, she says.

00:07:56.075 --> 00:07:59.712
But don't worry, we'll survive.

00:07:59.712 --> 00:08:01.214
Raya has lived in Krasnodar.

00:08:01.214 --> 00:08:03.783
Rivka all her life.

00:08:03.783 --> 00:08:05.818
Rustam and his colleagues venture out

00:08:05.818 --> 00:08:07.186
to these frontline villages

00:08:07.186 --> 00:08:08.654
several times a week,

00:08:08.654 --> 00:08:10.523
trying to convince people

00:08:10.523 --> 00:08:12.959
to move to safer ground.

00:08:12.959 --> 00:08:15.161
It's dangerous work, but first,

00:08:15.161 --> 00:08:16.229
it's worth the risk

00:08:16.229 --> 00:08:18.631
to get these children out of harm's way.

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:22.802
Looking into those eyes he asks,

00:08:22.802 --> 00:08:24.570
What else can you do

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:27.173
in is if friendly persuasion

00:08:27.173 --> 00:08:28.040
doesn't work?

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:30.576
There are other means.

00:08:30.576 --> 00:08:32.211
There's an order from local government

00:08:32.211 --> 00:08:33.613
requiring that children

00:08:33.613 --> 00:08:35.147
be evacuated from areas

00:08:35.147 --> 00:08:36.315
close to the fighting

00:08:37.283 --> 00:08:37.950
unit.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:38.284
This is

00:08:38.284 --> 00:08:39.085
how Vasily

00:08:39.085 --> 00:08:41.587
goes about the job of friendly persuasion

00:08:42.121 --> 00:08:43.322
Sitting, talking,

00:08:43.322 --> 00:08:44.824
trying to convince those

00:08:44.824 --> 00:08:47.393
who remain that their lives are in peril.

00:08:48.294 --> 00:08:49.629
The people in this basement

00:08:49.629 --> 00:08:51.097
turned bomb shelter

00:08:51.097 --> 00:08:53.633
have been down here for more than a year,

00:08:54.066 --> 00:08:56.636
and clearly that has taken a toll

00:08:59.539 --> 00:09:00.640
Their homes are here.

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:02.375
Everything they know is here.

00:09:02.375 --> 00:09:04.911
They refuse to leave.

00:09:04.911 --> 00:09:06.312
The eastern end of Krasnodar.

00:09:06.312 --> 00:09:08.381
Rivka is the hardest hit

00:09:08.381 --> 00:09:09.515
Yet even here,

00:09:09.515 --> 00:09:11.717
there's a stubborn holdout.

00:09:11.717 --> 00:09:12.985
They've come to this building

00:09:12.985 --> 00:09:15.755
to try to convince an old man to leave.

00:09:15.755 --> 00:09:18.057
They've already evacuated his wife.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:21.160
As you can see, this area has been

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:24.330
seriously smashed by incoming rounds.

00:09:25.131 --> 00:09:27.533
The Russians are just five kilometers

00:09:27.567 --> 00:09:30.069
around three miles from here.

00:09:30.069 --> 00:09:31.137
He didn't want his face

00:09:31.137 --> 00:09:32.338
to appear on camera.

00:09:33.839 --> 00:09:36.175
I'm not going anywhere, he says.

00:09:36.208 --> 00:09:37.243
I was born here

00:09:37.243 --> 00:09:40.379
and I'm going to die here.

00:09:40.379 --> 00:09:42.014
The chances of that happening

00:09:42.014 --> 00:09:44.483
here are perilously high.

00:09:47.353 --> 00:09:48.487
And what makes it even more

00:09:48.487 --> 00:09:49.555
perilous is the fact

00:09:49.555 --> 00:09:50.256
that the Russians

00:09:50.256 --> 00:09:53.292
are now using guided aerial bombs

00:09:53.292 --> 00:09:54.493
which can be launched

00:09:54.493 --> 00:09:57.663
50 kilometers from the front line.

00:09:57.930 --> 00:09:58.664
And the Russians

00:09:58.664 --> 00:10:00.800
apparently have no shortage

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:02.201
of those bombs.

00:10:02.201 --> 00:10:03.135
Alena

00:10:04.570 --> 00:10:05.805
All right, Ben Wedeman, thank you

00:10:05.805 --> 00:10:06.405
very much.

